older exam was a true mental  agility and endurance test there are 12  papers to be taken two a day for six  days it's a week-long marathon answering  hundreds of questions for five and a  half hours a day students trained for it  like an Olympic sport the highest  scoring student was called the senior  Wrangler and became a minor celebrity I  found the scores for an exam in the  1860s which gives an idea of scoring  around this time and out of a possible  Mark of 17  000 the senior Wrangler scored only  about 7 600 second place scored about 4  100 and the lowest scoring candidate to  still pass scored just 237 points and  earned the special wooden spoon award  the 1841 results are listed here with  Stokes the senior Wrangler that is  George Stone now famous for the navier  Stokes equation in fluid mechanics and  Stokes theorem in Vector calculus you  might have been examined on those ideas  yourself and now you've seen the exact  exam questions Stokes faced as a student  let's compare some similar questions  from then and now given that this exam  took place before Einstein's work on  relativity we can't expect much of an  analog to this general relativity  question but there are plenty of  questions about Newtonian gravity  1841 was before we developed  astronomical spectroscopy or measured  the expansion of the universe so this  cosmology question would blow the mind  of even an 1841 senior Wrangler but wait  actually George Stokes apparently is  credited with inventing the fundamental  principles of spectroscopy  modern quantum mechanics wasn't to be  invented for another 60 years so we  won't see that but there are plenty of  questions about light and we won't find  much machine learning statistical  modeling or coding and cryptography in  the 1841 paper since there were no  computers  these are the best I could find to  resemble the modern number Theory and  Analysis questions training for the  tripos has historically involved  external coaching to help students  increase the speed that they can solve  and write out Solutions and the whole  process has been criticized for not  allowing enough time for a deep  understanding or to make investigations  which are important skills for  mathematician and the senior Wrangler  has not always turned out to be the most  distinguished mathematician later in  life one notable critic of the tripos  was g h Hardy ramanujan's Mentor Hardy  gave an address to the mathematical  Association in 1926 calling to abolish  the tripos completely he said that the  ability to show originality in  mathematics can't be tested under exam  conditions and so the exam reduces to a  kind of game a student can choose to  play the game with all their Force but  must realize they are putting their  mathematical development on hold to do  so the prestige and status of the tripos  forces many students to devote  everything to the game  Hadi isn't against exams in general and  knows they are useful to test students  but he wants exams that do not profess  to be more than a reasonable test of  certain hum drum qualities the quality  is worth testing on an exam would carry  any student at Cambridge to second class  and beyond that he does not believe in  recognizing differences of ability by  examination the tripos is an exam that  attempted to sort students right to the  top today students are no longer  publicly ranked in order but the senior  Wrangler is still acknowledged during  the reading of results at Senate house  students today might still relate to the  idea of having to put their real  mathematical Pursuits on hold in order  to play the game Hardy says if Einstein  had taken the tripos what would it  matter what place he took  students are driven to perform in the  exams by tutors and greedy College  authorities I do not want to reform the  tripos but destroy it but neither I nor  anyone else will succeed in doing so  since the Practical difficulties would  be so serious and the force of tradition  is so terribly strong some things have  changed since 1926. Hardy's view is that  the tripods should produce research  mathematicians but not everyone studying  math has that aim the modern day tripos  website is proud that the course  prepares students for a range of jobs  not just Academia let me show you one  more interesting past paper this was the  first page of the tripos exam in 1890  and was the exam taken by Philippa  Fawcett she wasn't the first woman to  sit the math tripos but was the first to  rank number one as the results of the  exam were announced the men's result  adults were read first and then the  woman's women weren't officially ranked  but were placed relative to the men the  faucet was placed above the senior  Wrangler and Senate house erupted in  celebration she beat the senior Wrangler  by 400 marks and her success was  headline news it took another 58 years  before women were actually allowed to  receive degrees from Cambridge today the  results are read out in alphabetical  order rather than by rank but what do  you think does the tripos deserve to be  destroyed as Hardy wanted or is it a  worthy challenge that motivates students  to perform at their best  thanks for watching and a special thank  you to my patreon supporters including  today's patreon cats of the day pen and  tilt
 

